WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.724
Step four writes the next day's run with
the same inputs and a one-day window;

2
00:00:04.724 --> 00:00:07.100
it prints the same metrics and counts.

3
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.975
Step five packages both.

4
00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.437
The first package opens all
twenty counted findings.

5
00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:15.558
The second names the
first package's manifest,

6
00:00:15.558 --> 00:00:19.088
opens none and closes none,
because nothing changed.

7
00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:21.324
Verify rechecks the six files.

8
00:00:21.324 --> 00:00:26.075
Then the check an I S S O runs needs
nothing but the standard checksum tool:

9
00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:28.990
every file in the second
package reports OK.
